course: dictionary
lesson: 3726
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Flip is a word with several meanings, so you must read the words around it to know which one the writer means. «Swapping quickly between costumes, slightly different pictures of a sprite, makes animation, like a flip book.» Here a flip book has pages you turn quickly, so flip means to turn something over quickly.
explain: «Cockatoos ... learned to flip open wheelie bins» tells you that flip can also mean to turn or lift something quickly to open it. The bins are not being turned over like a pancake: the birds flick the lids open. Always ask what the word is doing in the sentence.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. «The gymnast did a flip on the mat» only makes sense if flip means a jump where you turn over in the air. If your meaning fits, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Flip means to turn something over quickly, like a coin or a pancake.
fact: A flip is a jump where you turn over in the air, like a gymnast.
fact: To flip a switch is to turn it on or off.
fact: To flip through a book is to turn its pages quickly.
fact: In maths, to flip a shape means to reflect it, like a mirror image, and it keeps the same size.
exercise: «The gymnast did a flip before landing on the mat.» What is a flip here? | A shape you reflect in maths | A switch you turn on or off | A page you turn quickly in a book | *A jump where you turn over in the air
exercise: In maths, what does it mean to flip a shape? | *Reflect it, like a mirror image, so it keeps its size | Make it bigger or smaller | Turn it over quickly like a pancake | Colour it in
exercise: «Cockatoos learned to flip open wheelie bins.» What does flip mean here? | *Turn or lift something quickly to open it | Count the bins one by one | Paint the bins bright colours | Jump high over the bins
test: «Please flip the switch to turn on the light.» What does flip mean here? | To jump high over it | To read the label quickly | To paint it a new colour | *To turn it on or off
test: In «males use them to wrestle, lifting and flipping rivals», what does flipping mean? | *Turning them over | Painting them | Counting them | Sleeping near them
exam: Which meaning of flip fits «She did a perfect flip on the mat»? | To reflect a shape in maths | To turn over quickly like a pancake | To turn a switch on or off | *A jump where you turn over in the air
